From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Date: Sat, 25 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] bcm283x: map DRAM above 4 GiB on BCM2711

bcm2711_mem_map only describes DRAM up to 0xfc000000 (the MMIO window base), so on
the 8 GiB Raspberry Pi 4 SKU U-Boot cannot touch the 0x1_00000000 - 0x2_00000000
half of memory at all: a fatload with a destination up there dies with
"Synchronous Abort ... Translation fault, level 1" even though
fdtdec_setup_memory_banksize() correctly reports the bank.

That matters for a Xen dom0less boot, where U-Boot has to place the hypervisor plus
one kernel/DTB/initramfs triple per domain before handing over. The RPi4 SoDeV
cockpit currently keeps every module below 0xfc000000 on purpose, but the low 4 GiB
is also where all of Dom0's and DomD's static memory lives, so the headroom is thin
and any additional dom0less guest has nowhere to go. This is the BCM2711
counterpart of the BCM2712 "expand MMU to 16 GB" change the RPi5 port carried for
exactly the same reason.

Add a fourth entry covering the upper 4 GiB as normal cacheable memory.
MEM_MAP_MAX_ENTRIES is 5 and bcm2711_mem_map used three entries plus the
terminator, so the table still fits without touching the bound.

On boards with less than 8 GiB the extra entry maps address space that has no DRAM
behind it. That is harmless: U-Boot only ever accesses memory it learned about from
the firmware device tree via bi_dram, and the LMB allocator is built from those
banks, so nothing dereferences the unbacked range.

Generated against xen-troops/u-boot branch rpi5-2024.04-xt
(arch/arm/mach-bcm283x/init.c), which is what recipes-bsp/u-boot/u-boot-src.inc
pins, so the hunk offsets match the tree bitbake unpacks.

Assisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-5
Signed-off-by: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [configuration]
---
 arch/arm/mach-bcm283x/init.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm/mach-bcm283x/init.c b/arch/arm/mach-bcm283x/init.c
--- a/arch/arm/mach-bcm283x/init.c
+++ b/arch/arm/mach-bcm283x/init.c
@@ -63,6 +63,16 @@
 			 PTE_BLOCK_NON_SHARE |
 			 PTE_BLOCK_PXN | PTE_BLOCK_UXN
 	}, {
+		/*
+		 * DRAM above the 4 GiB MMIO hole (8 GiB SKU). Needed so Xen
+		 * dom0less boot modules can be fatload'ed there.
+		 */
+		.virt = 0x100000000UL,
+		.phys = 0x100000000UL,
+		.size = 0x100000000UL,
+		.attrs = PTE_BLOCK_MEMTYPE(MT_NORMAL) |
+			 PTE_BLOCK_INNER_SHARE
+	}, {
 		/* List terminator */
 		0,
 	}
